-- T0b sql-truth baselines: hand-derived expected rows for archive/facts
-- corpus shapes where MemGQL's translation is NOT trusted.
--
-- As of the corpus-v2 recording (2026-07-06), ZERO archive/facts recipes
-- required sql-truth: every executable archive/facts shape is a simple
-- fixed-hop read or facts lookup that MemGQL translated correctly
-- (baseline=memgql, 28 entries). The one non-executable shape
-- (recipe_archive_topology_10, a WITH-aggregate rollup) is out of the
-- archive translator's scope by design and is a NEGATIVE shape
-- (expected ErrUnsupportedShape), not a result baseline.
--
-- If a future recipe lands whose MemGQL translation is suspect, record it
-- baseline=sql-truth in archive-result-goldens.json and add its
-- ground-truth SELECT here for the reviewer to fill expected_rows.
